# With no command, specval prints the usage to stderr and exits 2.
exits 2 sv
! stdout .
cmp stderr usage.txt

# help, -h, and --help print the usage to stdout and exit 0.
exits 0 sv help
cmp stdout usage.txt
! stderr .
exits 0 sv -h
cmp stdout usage.txt
exits 0 sv --help
cmp stdout usage.txt

# sv <command> --help and sv help <command> print the help of the command to
# stdout: the synopsis, the description, the flags, and the examples.
exits 0 sv check --help
cmp stdout check-help.txt
! stderr .
exits 0 sv help check
cmp stdout check-help.txt

# A flag that is not correct prints the error, the synopsis, and a pointer to
# --help to stderr, and exits 2.
exits 2 sv check --nope
! stdout .
cmp stderr check-flag.txt

# An unknown command prints an error and the usage, and exits 2.
exits 2 sv frobnicate
! stdout .
stderr '^unknown command "frobnicate"$'
stderr '^Usage:$'

-- usage.txt --
specval checks change specs against architecture rules before you write code.

Usage:
  sv check [--format text|json] [--strict] [files...]
        Check the given specs, or each spec in the specs directory.
        The exit status is 1 if a spec has an error, or a warning with --strict.
  sv context
        Print the spec format, the layers, the registry, and the rules.
        An agent reads this text before it writes a spec.
  sv new <id> [--kind feature|bugfix|chore] [--title "..."]
        Make the spec <specs dir>/<id>.yaml from the template.
  sv schema
        Print the JSON Schema of a spec.
  sv init [--dry-run]
        Set up specval, the Claude Code skill and hook, and the Copilot review
        instructions in this directory.
        You can run it again. It adds only the parts that are missing.
        With --dry-run, it prints the changes and writes nothing.
  sv doctor [--format text|json]
        Check the setup: the configuration, the rules, the registry, the
        Claude Code skill and hook, the Copilot review instructions, and the
        sv binary on PATH.
  sv version
        Print the version of sv and of the spec format.
  sv hook
        Claude Code runs this command after each file write. Do not run it yourself.
        If the file is a spec, specval checks it and sends the errors to Claude.

Run `sv <command> --help` for the flags and examples of a command.
-- check-help.txt --
Usage: sv check [--format text|json] [--strict] [files...]

Check the given specs, or each spec in the specs directory.
The exit status is 1 if a spec has an error, or a warning with --strict.

Flags:
  --format text|json
        the output format (default text)
  --strict
        exit with status 1 also for a warning

Examples:
  sv check
  sv check specs/ORD-143.yaml --format json
-- check-flag.txt --
flag provided but not defined: -nope
Usage: sv check [--format text|json] [--strict] [files...]
Run `sv check --help` for the flags and examples.
